WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:10.946
It was Christmas Eve.

2
00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:14.968
Speedy and Boomer were about to start their new job.

3
00:00:18.749 --> 00:00:20.929
The two reindeer looked around the warehouse.

4
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.970
They saw a huge, pretty sleigh.

5
00:00:28.471 --> 00:00:30.732
Colorful presents filled tall shelves.

6
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.262
Elves scurried around everywhere.

7
00:00:34.282 --> 00:00:37.004
"Hey there!"

8
00:00:37.344 --> 00:00:38.365
said a friendly voice.

9
00:00:39.946 --> 00:00:41.467
Speedy and Boomer turned around.

10
00:00:41.488 --> 00:00:45.571
"I'm Rudolph," said a reindeer with a shiny red nose.

11
00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:48.914
"I'm the reindeer in charge.

12
00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:54.358
Our job tonight is to pull that sleigh through the air."

13
00:00:54.378 --> 00:00:58.161
"That sounds easy," said Boomer.

14
00:00:59.242 --> 00:01:00.003
Rudolph nodded.

15
00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:01.404
"It's not hard.

16
00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:05.437
But our boss, Santa, has lots of stops to make.

17
00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:11.039
We'll stop at millions of houses all over the world."

18
00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:13.819
"Whoa!" Speedy gasped.

19
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.761
"One night isn't enough time!"

20
00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:21.602
"Don't worry," said Rudolph.

21
00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:24.803
"We will have 24 hours of night."

22
00:01:24.823 --> 00:01:27.563
"Huh?" said Boomer.

23
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:29.524
"How is that possible?"

24
00:01:38.772 --> 00:01:41.295
Rudolph led Boomer and Speedy to a giant map.

25
00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:50.723
"Earth is divided into 24 time zones," said Rudolph.

26
00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:55.748
"Because there are 24 hours in one day?"

27
00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:56.849
asked Speedy.

28
00:01:56.869 --> 00:01:59.291
"Right," said Rudolph.

29
00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:04.296
"The sun only shines on one side of Earth at a time.

30
00:02:05.096 --> 00:02:09.737
So it's always daytime in some places and nighttime in others."

31
00:02:10.898 --> 00:02:11.818
"Let me show you."

32
00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:14.479
Rudolph pressed a button.

33
00:02:15.539 --> 00:02:17.340
A big part of the map went dark.

34
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.001
"When it's 11:00 p.m.

35
00:02:22.161 --> 00:02:25.102
in Japan, it's only 11:00 a.m.

36
00:02:25.322 --> 00:02:27.362
in Argentina," Rudolph said.

37
00:02:27.382 --> 00:02:32.864
"Argentina's time is 12 hours behind Japan's."

38
00:02:34.828 --> 00:02:36.068
He pressed another button.

39
00:02:38.229 --> 00:02:39.609
A zigzag line appeared.

40
00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:44.031
"This is the International Date Line," said Rudolph.

41
00:02:44.051 --> 00:02:46.632
"Each day starts here.

42
00:02:47.612 --> 00:02:50.133
We'll start at this line and fly west."

43
00:02:55.914 --> 00:02:58.395
long will we spend in each time zone?"

44
00:02:58.795 --> 00:02:59.455
asked Speedy.

45
00:02:59.475 --> 00:03:01.216
"One hour.

46
00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:05.935
Then we'll move west to the next time zone," said Rudolph.

47
00:03:07.576 --> 00:03:10.578
"Oh! The time will be one hour earlier there!"

48
00:03:11.058 --> 00:03:11.619
said Boomer.

49
00:03:11.639 --> 00:03:15.061
"Exactly!" said Rudolph.

50
00:03:16.002 --> 00:03:17.023
"We should get ready.

51
00:03:17.323 --> 00:03:20.245
We have 24 time zones to visit!"

52
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:23.587
"That's a lot of flying," said Boomer.

53
00:03:23.607 --> 00:03:25.789
"I'm going to get hungry."

54
00:03:25.809 --> 00:03:30.212
"Many children leave treats for us," said Rudolph.

55
00:03:31.448 --> 00:03:35.032
"But watch out—the boss usually eats them all!"
